    {
      "id": "add-grouping-810910",
      "name": "AddGrouping",
      "category": "MovieSceneEntityGroupingSystem",
      "signature": "AddGrouping<GroupingPolicy>(Target, In Policy, In Components)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UMovieSceneEntityGroupingSystem*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Policy",
          "type": "GroupingPolicy&&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Components",
          "type": "TComponentTypeID<ComponentTypes> . . ."
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<GroupingPolicy,. . . ComponentTypes> FEntityGroupingPolicyKey",
      "docs": "Add a new grouping policy that will use the given components to make up a group key.\nGrouping policies must be simple structs that can be copied and owned by the grouping system, and\nthat implement the following members:\n- GroupKeyType [mandatory]\nA typedef or alias to the group key type to use to group entities together.\n- GetGroupKey(ComponentTypes... InComponents, GroupKeyType& OutGroupKey) [mandatory]\nA function that creates a group key used to group entities together.\nReturns true to indicate the key is valid, false otherwise. If false, the entity\ncorresponding to the given components will not be grouped.\n- OnObjectsReplaced(GroupKeyType& InOut, const TMap<UObject*, UObject*>&) [mandatory, sadly]\nPotentially changes a key if it contains a pointer to a replaced object. Should\nreturn true if any replacement occured.\n- PreTask() [optional]\nA function called before any grouping is done during an instantiation phase.\n- PostTask() [optional]\nA function called after any grouping is done dunring an instantiation phase.\n- PreProcessGroups() [optional]\n- PostProcessGroups() [optional]"
    },
